course: dictionary
lesson: 13541
title: Impound: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning the writer chose. Read the words around the word first, then try each meaning in the sentence to see which one fits.
explain: «The officers impounded the van because it was parked on the double yellow lines.» Here impound means to take something away and keep it until the rules are followed. The owner has to pay to get the van back. Think of a dog wearing no tag that is taken to a pound.
explain: «The engineers built a wall across the valley, and it impounded the river behind it.» This time impound means to hold water back, so a lake forms behind the wall. The river is not taken away. The clue is the water, the wall and the lake.
fact: Impound is a verb. Its other forms are impounds, impounded and impounding.
fact: «Impound» means to take something away and keep it until the rules are followed, such as a car, a dog or goods.
fact: «Impound» can also mean to hold water back behind a dam or wall, which makes a reservoir.
fact: «Impounded vehicle» is a phrase for a car or van that has been taken away and kept by officials.
fact: Use the clues in the sentence, such as «van», «dam» or «water», to choose the right meaning.
exercise: «The council impounded the car that was parked on the yellow lines.» What does impounded mean here? | *Took it away and kept it until the rules were followed | Painted it bright red | Sold it to a friend | Washed it and gave it back the same day
exercise: «The dam impounded the river, and a huge lake formed behind the wall.» What does impounded mean here? | *Held the water back behind the wall | Drained the lake dry | Turned the river into the sea | Made the river run faster
exercise: «The officers impounded the van and took it to the pound.» Which word names the thing that was taken away? | pound | officers | *van | impounded
test: «The stray dog was impounded by the council until its owner came to collect it.» What does impounded mean? | Given a new home straight away | *Taken away and kept by officials | Fed and walked around the park | Let loose in the fields
test: «The engineers impounded the stream to make a reservoir for the town.» What does impounded mean? | Painted the wall | *Held the water back behind a dam | Dried up the stream | Let the stream run wild
exam: Which two meanings does impound have? | Count coins; send letters by post | Buy and sell goods at a market; shout loudly and run fast | *Take something away until the rules are followed; hold water back behind a dam | Hide a treasure under the ground; plant seeds in spring
